'' THREE SPELLINGS THE CORPUS WRITES AND NOTHING READ.
''
'' 'integer<8>=' lexes the closing '>' and the '=' as ONE '>=' token, so the sized
'' type went unparsed and its constant had no value -- which declines at every use.
'' numbers/integer_n.bas writes every one of its constants that way.
''
'' 'unsigned' is the first word of a two-word type name, so 'sizeof( unsigned
'' integer )' was read as an expression and failed at the second word. Measured: 8, 1,
'' 2, 2 for the four below.
''
'' '@( @x )' over a BYREF PARAMETER is the parameter's own slot -- a byref parameter
'' IS a pointer variable, so '@x' names its contents. Measured, and fbc REJECTS the
'' same spelling over any other variable (error 24), so there is nothing else beside
'' it. pointers/arith.bas puts every byref case through one macro that writes it four
'' times.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/sized-int-unsigned.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/sized-int-unsigned.out
